# Wolseley 21/60 six-light saloon, 1929-1935.
#
# The 2,677 cc six of 1929-35. The research corrected the order's date: the
# 21/60 is NOT a 1938-48 car. From 1936 the large six was the '21' (2,916
# cc), and the 1938-48 large Wolseley was the 25 hp.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseley_21/60
#
# Dimensions: not established. The model measures 4.44 x 1.68 x 1.79 m on a
# 2.85 m wheelbase, ESTIMATED from the photographs and an assumed 0.74 m tyre
# diameter; these are not specifications and must not be quoted as such.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a front three-quarter of a 1934 21/60 County
# six-light saloon; there is no true side profile. The flank is estimated
# from the two images and the published proportions. The limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period chart was found. Black, grey, green and
# maroon are plain names. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 120 km/h. Comfort 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 2,3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 1929 intro, retires staggered 1950-1953.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/wolseley-21-60.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/wolseley-21-60.dae. References:
# citycars/references/wolseley-21-60/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: neither photograph is side-on, so the flank is estimated.
# The running boards, bustle and rear window are simplified. At 128 px the tall
# six-light cabin, upright grille and side spare read as a 21/60 County.


obj=citycar
